em looks as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069697/assets/f2b5b95167b1ecd07aa1152aeac6dd454fbe71ba953b05c4da22d8c36f76277a.png)" 13194139535705 true] [17592186362266 1113 #uuid "ce2b17fe-4288-536e-8944-f1f7021c8fc9" 13194139535705 true] [17592186362266 1145 "Since we have a repeated eigenvalue $\\lambda =-3$ (of multiplicity two) and only one corresponding eigenvector $v,$ the solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}v{e}^{\\lambda t}+{c}_{2}(vt{e}^{\\lambda t}+w{e}^{\\lambda t}\\,),\n$$\n\nwhere $w$ is a solution to the equation $(A-\\lambda I)w=v.$\n\nIn our case, \n\n$$\n\\lambda =-3,\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \nThus, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}] & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}+{c}_{2}([\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]t{e}^{-3t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}{e}^{-3t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{-3t}[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{-3t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the $x\\text{-axis}.$ Since ${e}^{-3t}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions approach $\\text{the origin}$ as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069697/assets/8dc90697da27e52e0c1818d5529247d132944f30603936bedc191c4a14cb7d9c.png)\n\nNow, consider solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{-3t}[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\nWhen ${c}_{2}=1,$ we get the following curve:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=t{e}^{-3t} \\\\ y={e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the coordinates (rounded to two decimal places) of several points on the curve, we get the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $-0.5$ | $0$ | $0.5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-2.24$ | $0$ | $0.11$ |\n| $y$ | $4.48$ | $1$ | $0.22$ |\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069697/assets/3981c3c5bdfc66850798ee3c34031acb0d1cdfea7181eb34a0a0422b44cc2ef0.png)\n\nThe phase portrait of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14069697/assets/f2b5b95167b1ecd07aa1152aeac6dd454fbe71ba953b05c4da22d8c36f76277a.png)" 13194139535705 true] [17592186362267 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362268 13194139535705 true] [17592186362267 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362269 13194139535705 true] [17592186362267 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362270 13194139535705 true] [17592186362267 1000 #edb/ref 17592186362271 13194139535705 true] [17592186362267 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139535705 true] [17592186362267 1041 "field-1" 13194139535705 true] [17592186362267 1104 #edb/ref 17592186362270 13194139535705 true] [17592186362267 1110 #uuid "5abf3e04-df2a-525b-b0c6-31baf754557a" 13194139535705 true] [17592186362268 1034 "t{e}^{3t}" 13194139535705 true] [17592186362268 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535705 true] [17592186362268 1111 #uuid "3b7edf28-79ce-5d95-99e6-1749b04897a6" 13194139535705 true] [17592186362269 1034 "{e}^{3t}" 13194139535705 true] [17592186362269 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535705 true] [17592186362269 1111 #uuid "f392b40e-7bb1-5b54-abbe-b3f6869e1e67" 13194139535705 true] [17592186362270 1034 "t{e}^{-3t}" 13194139535705 true] [17592186362270 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535705 true] [17592186362270 1111 #uuid "e627b0b4-25d8-5d2e-ad48-e2bd5b5752ed" 13194139535705 true] [17592186362271 1034 "{e}^{-3t}" 13194139535705 true] [17592186362271 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535705 true] [17592186362271 1111 #uuid "e9